  triage:title "Missing compatibility matrix tests for CompatibilityVerdict admission — CLOSED" ;
  triage:description "Sprint doc's 'Required validation' section explicitly required compatibility matrix tests covering: release mismatch, schema mismatch, HTTP-major mismatch, same-major minor/patch interoperability. Fix commit 77252eca adds compatibility_admission_matrix_ignores_release_and_checks_schema_and_http_major at crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health.rs:1136-1189. Independently verified CLOSED by two reviewers: req-qa (direct source read) and rust-qa-agent (ran cargo test --workspace, confirmed the test executes and passes, quoted the full test body). The test calls the real DaemonRequestDispatcher::compatibility_verdict function (not a mock) and asserts all four required scenarios: release mismatch (9.9.9-beta.1, remains Compatible - confirms release is correctly ignored), same-major differing minor/patch HTTP version (1.99.7 vs HTTP_API_VERSION, remains Compatible), schema mismatch (CLI_SCHEMA_VERSION+1, returns Incompatible with schema_version fields differing), and HTTP-major mismatch (2.0.0, returns Incompatible with major() differing). cargo test confirmed this test passes (0 failed across test results workspace-wide)." ;
